// event: completion A A.x
// concurrent: completion A A.x; completion A B.v
// note: a lock order that is no dependency cycle: A.x (in class A) needs B.v, and B.v needs object A's p, a chain x -> v -> p. With a root per fact no pair of safepoints finds a cycle. With a class and its companion one root (the loader's), reader A holds pair A inside x while it waits for pair B, and reader B holds pair B inside v and asks for pair A to complete object A: a wait-for cycle the sequential run never has; RAISE reports it as a cyclic reference (I54, lesson 6), VICTIM aborts and retries the reader that closes it
// file: A
class Int {}
object A { def p: Int }
class A { def x = M.m.v }
object B { def v = N.n.p }
object M { def m = B }
object N { def n = A }
